  "pages": 15,
  "question": "What exact denominator obstructions are checked for Erdős #68, and which quantified producer could still prove irrationality?",
  "precis": "The paper proves that if S=a/q is rational, q cannot divide 299999! and is at least 2^39990 > 10^12038. The first exclusion comes from the exact strict-successor carry test and the second from continued fractions. Lean also checks the equivalent carry formulation and several consequences. A large common denominator alone does not control the reduced partial sums. Irrationality is reduced to a cofinal miss of the strict factorial successor, which remains open.",
  "owns": "the problem-specific exposition for Erdős #68: exact factorial normal forms, structural consumers, finite denominator evidence, method boundaries, and five ranked open producers",
